1031:### Iframe support
1032-
1033:Iframes are detected automatically during snapshots. When the main-frame snapshot runs, `Iframe` nodes are resolved and their content is inlined beneath the iframe element in the output (one level of nesting; iframes within iframes are not expanded).
1034-
1035-```bash
1036-agent-browser snapshot -i
1037:# @e3 [Iframe] "payment-frame"
1038-#   @e4 [input] "Card number"
1039-#   @e5 [button] "Pay"
1040-
1041:# Interact directly — refs inside iframes already work
1042-agent-browser fill @e4 "4111111111111111"
1043-agent-browser click @e5
1044-
1045:# Or switch frame context for scoped snapshots
1046:agent-browser frame @e3               # Switch using element ref
1047:agent-browser snapshot -i             # Snapshot scoped to that iframe
1048:agent-browser frame main              # Return to main frame
1049-```
1050-
1051:The `frame` command accepts:
1052:- **Element refs** — `frame @e3` resolves the ref to an iframe element
1053:- **CSS selectors** — `frame "#payment-iframe"` finds the iframe by selector
1054:- **Frame name/URL** — matches against the browser's frame tree
